<title>UK: Rhone-Poulenc says UK EMU stance worrying.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc says UK EMU stance worrying.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British arm of French chemicals group Rhone Poulenc SA said on Wednesday that Britain's uncertainty about a single European currency was worrying its parent company and might discourage investment in Britain.</p>
<p>Chris Andrews, chairman and managing director of Rhone-Poulenc Ltd, told the Chemical Industries Association (CIA) investment intentions conference: &quot;I get the impression talking to many French colleagues that uncertaintly about the UK position on EMU is worrying them, and can only act as some kind of discouragement to investment in the future.&quot;</p>
</text>
